  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVING PATAGONIA THROUGH WILDLIFE FRIENDLY AND CLIMATE SMART LIVESTOCK HUSBANDRY</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THIS PROJECT BUILDS ON THE STRATEGIC ALLIANCE BETWEEN THE USFWS AND WCS TO CONSOLIDATE AND EXPAND WILDLIFE-FRIENDLY AND CLIMATE-SMART LIVESTOCK MANAGEMENT IN THREE CRITICAL LANDSCAPES IN THE PATAGONIAN REGION OF ARGENTINA AND CHILE. WE SEEK TO IMPROVE THE CONSERVATION AND CLIMATE RESILIENCE OF THE ENTIRE REGIONAL WILDLIFE ASSEMBLAGE (INCLUDING GUANACOS, RHEAS, ANDEAN CATS, PUMAS, CULPEO AND CHILLA FOXES AND CONDORS). THIS WILDLIFE IS CURRENTLY THREATENED BY HUNTING AND PERSECUTION BY PRODUCERS AND FREE-ROAMING DOGS, COMPETITION WITH LIVESTOCK FOR PASTURESAND WATER, AND HABITAT DEGRADATION BY LIVESTOCK, ALL IN A SCENARIO OF CHANGING CLIMATIC CONDITIONS THAT REDUCE PRODUCTIVITY THROUGH MUCH OF THE REGION. SEVERAL GOVERNMENT AND PRIVATE INITIATIVES IN THE PATAGONIAN REGION SEEK TO INCREASE RESILIENCE OF HABITATS AND RURAL LIVELIHOODS IN THE FACE OF CLIMATE CHANGE THROUGH BETTER GRAZING MANAGEMENT STRATEGIES THAT ALLOW VEGETATION AND SOILS TO RECOVER AND OR THE DEVELOPMENT OF ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS, SUCH AS GUANACO MEAT AND FIBER, BUT THESE INITIATIVES DO NOT PRIORITIZE WILDLIFE CONSERVATION. WE WILL EXPAND OURWILDLIFE-FRIENDLY APPROACH DEVELOPED UNDER THE USFWS-WCS COOPERATIVE AGREEMENT TO CREATE A MORE COMPREHENSIVE WILDLIFE-FRIENDLY CLIMATE-SMART MODEL FOR LIVESTOCK AND WILDLIFE COEXISTENCE IN PATAGONIA. THIS WIL</narrative>
  </description>
